{title: Run}
{artist: Hozier}
{key: Am}

{c: Verse 1}
[Am],        Rare is this love, keep it covered
[Am] [G] [Em] [F],        I need you to run to me, run to me, lover
[F] [Am],        Run until you feel your lungs bleeding
[Am],        Oh, but the farrow know
[G],        Her hungry eye, her ancient soul
[Em],        Its carried by the sneering menagerie
[Am],        Know what it is to grow
Beneath her sky, a punishing cold,        [G] [Em]
To slowly learn of her ancient misery,        [F] [G]
To be twisted by something,        C [F]
A shame without a sin,        Like how she twisted the bog man
[G],        After she married him
[Am],        Rare is this love, keep it covered
[Am] [G] [Em] [F],        I need you to run to me, run to me, lover
[F] [Am],        Run until you feel your lungs bleeding
[Am],        But in all the world
There is one lover worthy of her,        [G] [Em]
With as many souls claimed as she,        [Am]
But for all hes worth,        He still shatters always on her earth
[G] [Em],        The cause of every tear shed ever weep
[F] [G],        Rushing ashore to meet her
C [F],        Foaming with loneliness
White hands to fondle and beat her,        [G]
Give her his onliness,        [Am]
Rare is this love, keep it covered,        [Am] [G] [Em] [F]
I need you to run to me, run to me, lover,        [F] [Am]
Run until you feel your lungs bleeding
